<!--
  Over Strike 2 - the in-game HUD (custom_hud_layout, CS2 update of 2026-08-24).

  Structure and style only: every word that can change comes from the GunGameWelcome plugin as a dialog variable ({s:text} on a
  labelled panel; the words live in bridge/Hud.cs), and every state (window open, page, card, votes) is a class the plugin
  sets - for everybody on gg_global, per player on gg_screen. The bridge's selftest checks that every id and class the plugin
  sends exists here and in the stylesheet, and that every {s:text} label here is fed.

  Rules from CS2UIKit's GOTCHAS (MIT) that this file obeys, because each one makes CS2 drop the whole layout without a word:
  the root panel has no id; only Panel, Label, Image and Button; no inline style; no scaling attribute; pictures are panel
  backgrounds, never <Image src="...vsvg">.

  Release v3_0_0 (2026-10-21): the HUD is the server's whole interface - there are no chat commands any more. On one full-screen root:
    1. the board  - beside the scoreboard while TAB is held (the client's own HUD_SCOREBOARD_VISIBLE class shows it). With the TAB
       cursor (HUD_TAB down) it is a click action panel: your vote on the map that is on, Next (a random map, I'm done, or vote to
       skip), the queue in one line, and the full menu;
    2. the card   - "now playing" at each map's first spawn, "welcome back" on a returning player's join;
    3. the banner - a map change counting down;
    4. the news   - one line for everybody: what just happened (a pick, a skip vote, the queue moving, a crash, a restart);
    5. the note   - one line for one player: the answer to their own click (a refusal, a confirmation to give);
    6. the window - the full menu: start, the map browser (full-text search on an on-screen keyboard, a card for a Workshop id that is
       not on the list), the queue, game settings, help and rules, with the live map state and clickable votes beside them.

  Map thumbnails are classes on the cards' gg_m1_thumb ... gg_m8_thumb: two per picture, th(n / 64) and tl(n % 64), n being the map's
  number in bridge/HudThumbList.cs (two out of a small set, because the game takes at most 1,024 class names per layout entity).
  Each pair is a rule in gungame_hud_thumbs.css that points at a JPEG in the addon (or at the game's own picture of an official map).
-->
<root>
	<styles>
		<include src="s2r://panorama/styles/custom_game/gungame_hud_v3_0_0.vcss_c" />
		<include src="s2r://panorama/styles/custom_game/gungame_hud_thumbs_v3_0_0.vcss_c" />
	</styles>

	<Panel class="gg-root" hittest="false">
		<Panel id="gg_global" class="gg-global" hittest="false">
			<Panel id="gg_screen" class="gg-screen" hittest="false">

				<!-- 1. The board: TAB. A click action panel while the TAB cursor is on (HUD_TAB down): vote, Next, the queue, the menu. -->
				<Panel class="gg-board" hittest="false">
					<Panel class="gg-board-head">
						<Panel class="gg-knife gg-knife-small" />
